\subsection{Floquet Magnus expansion}
The Floquet Magnus expansion is a perturbative method to obtain the stroboscopic Floquet effective Hamiltonian $H_F$ for a periodically driven system. The method is based on the Magnus expansion \cite{magnus} which is a series expansion of the time-ordered exponential. The Floquet Magnus expansion is given by, 
\begin{equation}
    e^{-iH_F\tau}=T\exp\left(-i\int_0^\tau dt\,H(t)\right)
\end{equation}
where $T$ denotes time ordering. The Floquet Magnus expansion yields $H_F$ as a series in inverse drive frequency $\tau^{-1}$. The first few terms in the expansion are given by, 
\begin{eqnarray}
H_F^{(0)}&=&\frac{1}{\tau}\int_0^\tau dt\,H(t)\nonumber\\
H_F^{(1)}&=&\frac{1}{2\tau^2}\int_0^\tau dt\int_0^t ds\,[H(t),H(s)]\

