$, one can note, that by the order of magnitude $d/d\ell\sim k$, where $k$ is a wavenumber, describing the propagation of the polaritons along the waveguide. Therefore, for narrow waveguides and small $k$, when $k\ll d^{-1}$, these terms can be neglected as compared to $\Omega_\pm$, and one gets the Hamiltonian (4) of the main text.


