\subsection*{B}
We shall prove that $M$ is non-decreasing in the untrapped region.
In the untrapped region, we have $\vartheta_{\pm} \geq 0$.
Then the dominant energy condition implies that
\begin{equation}
\partial_{\pm}M \geq 0.
\end{equation}
This means that $M$ is non-decreasing in the untrapped region.
In the trapped region, we have $\vartheta_{\pm} < 0$.
Then the dominant energy condition implies that
\begin{equation}
\partial_{\pm}M \leq 0.
\end{equation}
This means that $M$ is non-increasing in the trapped region.
Thus we have proved that $M$ is non-decreasing in the untrapped region
and non-increasing in the trapped region.

