\section{Conclusion}
\label{Concl}
We have shown that the local energy change in a composite system is given by the sum of the local energy changes of the subsystems. This result is valid for arbitrary local Hamiltonians and arbitrary local Lindblad operators. The result is derived from the general form of the local energy change and the subsystem Lindblad equations. The result is important for the understanding of energy changes in open quantum systems and for the development of efficient simulation methods for open quantum systems.

