This bound is valid for any $\rho$ and $\sigma$ and any low-rank matrix $A$. For the special case of $\rho=\sigma$, the error simplifies to

\begin{align}
\epsilon_{\rho,\rho} \leq 3 \Vert A \Vert_{\max}^2.
\end{align}

This error bound is independent of the dimension $N$ and the rank $r$ of $A$. It is also independent of the choice of $\rho$ and $\sigma$. The error bound is thus a direct consequence of the properties of the modified swap matrix. The bound is tight, as can be seen by considering the case where $A$ is a diagonal matrix with all elements equal to $\Vert A \Vert_{\max}$. In this case, the error is exactly $3 \Vert A \Vert_{\max}^2$.

