4L}\int_0^Td\sigma_1\int_0^Td\sigma_2B(\sigma_1,\sigma_2|\tau_1,\tau_2)
x(\sigma_1)\cdot x(\sigma_2), 
\end{equation}
with $ B(\sigma_1,\sigma_2|\tau_1,\tau_2)$ as given by eq. (82), we are
led to the equations of motion given by eq. (81) in the text. Considering a solution of the form $x_\mu=\eta_\mu+z_\mu$, with $\eta_\mu$
as in (56) we are led to the relation (we drop, as in the text, the
$\tau$-arguments in $B$)
\begin{equation}
\int_0^Td\sigma'\left[\delta(\sigma-\sigma')\frac{\partial^2}{\partial 
\sigma'^2}-
{1\over L}B(\sigma',\sigma)\right]z_\mu(\sigma')= [\delta(\sigma-\tau_2)
-\delta(\sigma-\tau_1)](\tau_1-\tau_2)\frac{u_\mu}{L} 
