\section{Conclusion}
\label{conclusion}
In this paper, we have presented a novel approach for learning cue-specific and shared embedding spaces for emotion recognition. Our experiments demonstrate the effectiveness of our method in capturing the nuances of different cues and leveraging them for emotion recognition. By learning cue-specific embeddings, we are able to capture the unique characteristics of each cue, while learning shared embeddings allows us to exploit the commonalities across cues. Our transfer learning experiments further show the potential of our method in adapting to new cues and domains. Future work will focus on extending our method to handle multimodal inputs and exploring the use of more sophisticated neural network architectures.

