\subsection{Cloning rate and cloning probability distribution function}

The cloning rate $\Gamma(\lambda)$ is defined as the rate at which
trajectories with Lyapunov exponent $\lambda$ are cloned. From the
previous section, it is clear that $\Gamma(\lambda)$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\Gamma(\lambda) = \alpha \lambda^* + f(\lambda^*)
