\subsection{Vilkovisky-DeWitt effective action}
The VD effective action is defined as a functional of the classical fields and is invariant under field reparametrizations. The VD effective action is obtained by integrating out the quantum fluctuations around a given classical background field configuration. The VD effective action is given by:
\[
\Gamma[\phi_c] = \int \mathcal{D}\phi \, \ln \mathcal{D}\phi \, e^{iS[\phi]}
\]
