\subsection{Embedding in supergravity}
The embedding of VSI spacetimes in supergravity theories is a natural extension of the study of these spacetimes. The presence of additional fields, such as the gravitino and the dilaton, can lead to new solutions and interesting physical phenomena. For instance, the presence of a dilaton field can lead to the existence of naked singularities in certain cases \cite{dilaton}. In the context of higher dimensional supergravity, the embedding of VSI spacetimes can be achieved by considering the appropriate field equations and ensuring that the additional fields are compatible with the VSI condition. This involves solving the field equations for the metric and the other fields, and checking that the curvature invariants remain zero.

