\section*{Space-time crystal dynamics}
The tight-binding Hamiltonian derived in the previous section can be used to study the dynamics of space-time crystals. The time evolution of the system is governed by the Schr\"odinger equation, $\partial_t \ket{\psi(t)} = H \ket{\psi(t)}$. For a space-time crystal, the system exhibits periodic dynamics with a period $T = 2\pi/\Omega$. To analyze the dynamics, we can perform a Floquet analysis, which involves transforming the time-dependent Hamiltonian into a time-independent form. The Floquet Hamiltonian is given by
\begin{equation}
    \hat{H}_{\text{Floquet}} = \hat{H} - i\hbar \frac{\partial}{\partial t},
\end{equation}
where $\hat{H}$ is the time-dependent Hamiltonian obtained from the tight-binding representation. The eigenstates of the Floquet Hamiltonian are Floquet states, which are characterized by quasienergies. The quasienergy spectrum provides information about the stability and dynamical properties of the space-time crystal.

