\section{Conclusion}\label{section:conclusion}

In this work, we proposed a novel approach for the imputation of missing values in fMRI data. Our method leverages the spatial and temporal dimensions of the data to provide accurate imputations. We validated our approach on multiple datasets and compared it to state-of-the-art baselines. The results show that our method outperforms the baselines in terms of imputation accuracy and robustness to missing data. Future work will focus on extending our approach to handle more complex missing patterns and integrating it with other neuroimaging analysis pipelines.

